course: dictionary
lesson: 9261
title: Which way is south?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: South is one of the four main directions: north, south, east and west. On most maps, south is at the bottom, and it is the opposite of north.
explain: South is opposite to north, so walking south takes you back towards where you started from the north. Walk 5 steps north, then 3 steps south, and you are 2 steps north of your start. The south takes away from the north.
explain: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» Here South America is a name for a continent, and it is the part of the Americas that lies to the south. Its capital S shows that it is a name, not just a direction.
explain: The Sun can help you find south. «At midday in Britain the Sun is in the south, so shadows point north.» Shadows fall the opposite way to the Sun, so a shadow at midday points north.
fact: South is one of the four main compass directions: north, south, east and west.
fact: The south of a place is the part that lies in that direction, as in «the south of England».
fact: South can also mean moving towards the south, as in «we travelled south».
fact: The South Pole is the most southern point of the Earth, in Antarctica.
fact: In December the southern half of the world has summer, and Australia and New Zealand are in the south.
exercise: On most maps, which way is south? | Up, at the top | Right, towards the east | *Down, at the bottom | Left, towards the west
exercise: In «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America», what is South America? | The northern part of the Americas | *The southern part of the Americas | The Sun's position at night | The eastern coast of the sea
exercise: Ben walks 5 steps north, then 3 steps south. Where is he now, compared with his start? | 2 steps south | 8 steps north | *2 steps north | 5 steps south
test: At midday in Britain the Sun is in the south. Which way do the shadows point? | East | West | *North | South
test: South-west lies between which two directions? | *South and west | North and east | South and east | North and west
exam: The South Pole is the most southern point of the Earth, and it is found in which continent? | Asia | Africa | Europe | *Antarctica
